Write a function sum4_mod that takes five unsigned 32-bit numbers a, b, c, d, m and returns the sum of a, b, c, d modulo m, as an unsigned 32-bit number. Put a, b, c, d in that order into a sequence of four unsigned 32-bit numbers and pass it to a helper function sum4(v) that returns the sum of the four values of v as an unsigned 64-bit number; write and use that helper. When m is 0 the function must stop with trap kind 2 (division by zero).
